{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function createHeldKeys(): () => string[];","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/solid-hotkeys/src/createHeldKeys.ts#L26","children":[{"type":"text","value":"createHeldKeys.ts:26"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SolidJS primitive that returns a signal of currently held keyboard keys."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This primitive uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useSelector"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/solid-store"},{"type":"text","value":" to subscribe\nto the global KeyStateTracker and updates whenever keys are pressed\nor released."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Signal accessor for array of currently held key names"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"() => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":"[]"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function KeyDisplay() {\n  const heldKeys = createHeldKeys()\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      Currently pressed: {heldKeys().join(' + ') || 'None'}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction createHeldKeys(): () => string[];\n```\n\nDefined in: [createHeldKeys.ts:26](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/solid-hotkeys/src/createHeldKeys.ts#L26)\n\nSolidJS primitive that returns a signal of currently held keyboard keys.\n\nThis primitive uses `useSelector` from `@tanstack/solid-store` to subscribe\nto the global KeyStateTracker and updates whenever keys are pressed\nor released.\n\n## Returns\n\nSignal accessor for array of currently held key names\n\n() => `string`[]\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\nfunction KeyDisplay() {\n  const heldKeys = createHeldKeys()\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      Currently pressed: {heldKeys().join(' + ') || 'None'}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: createHeldKeys\ntitle: createHeldKeys\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction createHeldKeys(): () => string[];\n```\n\nDefined in: [createHeldKeys.ts:26](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/solid-hotkeys/src/createHeldKeys.ts#L26)\n\nSolidJS primitive that returns a signal of currently held keyboard keys.\n\nThis primitive uses `useSelector` from `@tanstack/solid-store` to subscribe\nto the global KeyStateTracker and updates whenever keys are pressed\nor released.\n\n## Returns\n\nSignal accessor for array of currently held key names\n\n() => `string`[]\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\nfunction KeyDisplay() {\n  const heldKeys = createHeldKeys()\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      Currently pressed: {heldKeys().join(' + ') || 'None'}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n"}
